MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The hose clamps felt useful because I have bought them repeatedly for repair work; another adjustable set connects to a demonstrated need.",
    "The epoxy fits my history of buying strong tape and repair adhesive, while the rubber grommets offer a practical complement to my wire connectors by protecting wiring through holes."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The nuts, thread gauge, and caliper could be useful for repairs, but I have no specific fastening or measuring task that would make me choose them now.",
    "The casters and cutting wheels depend on a project and compatible equipment I have not established. Copper tape serves conductive or shielding purposes that my duct tape purchases do not imply, and the medical test has no clear connection to my repair needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying repair supplies seems to have been taken as a reason to recommend a broad range of workshop tools, even when their jobs differ from mine.",
    "Surface similarities seem to carry too much weight: buying duct tape does not establish a need for conductive tape, and buying a handtruck does not establish a need for replacement casters."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated hose clamp purchases give a clearer indication of an ongoing need than a single purchase of equipment such as the handtruck.",
    "The intended repair and fit matter to me: clamp diameter, adhesive suitability, and wiring protection provide concrete reasons to buy, while a vaguely related tool does not."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my practical repair needs but stretch them into specialized tools and supplies without a clear current use."
}
